# This layer no longer uses terraform.tfvars.
#
# Normal configuration - region, org_prefix, kubernetes_version, node sizing and
# authentication_mode - lives in ../config.yaml, which is committed.
#
# Two values are not committed, because both carry the account id. Supply them
# from the gitignored ../.env:
#
#   source ../.env
#   terraform plan
#
# ../.env should contain:
#
#   export TF_VAR_account_id=REPLACE-WORKLOAD-ACCOUNT-ID
#   export TF_VAR_admin_principal_arns='["arn:aws:iam::<account>:role/aws-reserved/sso.amazonaws.com/AWSReservedSSO_<prefix>-PlatformEngineer_<suffix>"]'
#
# Note the HCL list syntax on the second one - shell array syntax will not parse.
#
# The AWSReservedSSO_ suffix is generated by AWS. Read it off your own session
# with `aws sts get-caller-identity`, but rebuild it in the iam role form above -
# the sts assumed-role ARN that command prints is not what EKS access entries
# accept.
#
# authentication_mode is API, so an empty admin list means nobody can reach the
# cluster once it exists.
#
# This file is kept as a pointer only; a terraform.tfvars here would still be
# auto-loaded and would override the config above.
